---
layout: layouts/dnd-index.njk
title: D&D
eyebrow: Campaign canon
lead: Agdaron is the homebrew world my group has been playing in since 2019, and The Undying of the Light is the campaign that has been running through it. Campaigns first, then the lore behind them, then the characters who keep breaking both.
description: Campaign canon for Agdaron, the homebrew D&D world Muqtadaa Miandara runs, and The Undying of the Light, the campaign set in it. Campaigns, lore and characters, with the drawings made for the table.
---
{% import "macros/section-header.njk" as headers %}

{#-
  One group per post type (lib/dnd.js POST_TYPES order: Campaigns, Lore,
  Characters), newest post first; a type with no posts is skipped. Posts come
  from src/dnd/posts/ (see src/dnd/README.md).
-#}
{%- set groups = collections.dndPost | dndGroups %}
{%- set cardSizes = "(min-width: 64em) 26rem, (min-width: 40em) 50vw, 100vw" %}
{%- if groups.length %}
{%- for group in groups %}
<section class="section" data-bg="bone" data-py="lg"{% if not loop.first %} data-border="top"{% endif %} aria-labelledby="group-{{ group.type.id }}">
  <div class="container stack-8">
    {#- No eyebrow: "Lore" above "Lore" is the section title said twice. -#}
    {{ headers.sectionHeader(title='<span id="group-' + group.type.id + '">' + group.type.plural + '</span>', description=group.type.description, size="md") }}
    <ul class="grid grid-3" role="list">
      {%- for post in group.posts %}
      <li>
        <a class="post-card" href="{{ post.url }}">
          {%- if post.data.coverItem %}
          {%- set cover = post.data.coverItem %}
          <div class="post-card__media"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="{{ cover.webpSrcset }}" sizes="{{ cardSizes }}"><img src="{{ cover.thumb }}" srcset="{{ cover.srcset }}" sizes="{{ cardSizes }}" width="{{ cover.width }}" height="{{ cover.height }}" alt="{{ cover.alt }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></picture></div>
          {%- endif %}
          <div class="post-card__body">
            <p class="post-card__eyebrow eyebrow-wide">{{ post.data.type | dndTypeLabel }}{% if post.date %} · <time datetime="{{ post.date | isoDate }}">{{ post.date | readableDate }}</time>{% endif %}</p>
            <p class="post-card__title">{{ post.data.title }}</p>
            {%- if post.data.summary %}<p class="post-card__summary">{{ post.data.summary }}</p>{% endif %}
          </div>
        </a>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}

{#-
  From the sketchbook: art tagged `dnd` in gallery/art/captions.yml, up to
  eight pieces. Each tile links to /art/#<slug>, which opens the gallery
  lightbox on that piece.
-#}
{%- set sketches = galleries.art | withTag("dnd") | limit(8) %}
{%- set sketchSizes = "(min-width: 40em) 16rem, 60vw" %}
{#- Nothing tagged `dnd` renders no strip at all; check-gallery.mjs warns the
    author at build time instead of the page apologising to the reader. -#}
{%- if sketches.length %}
<section class="section" data-bg="linen" data-py="lg">
  <div class="container stack-8">
    <div class="row-between">
      {{ headers.sectionHeader(eyebrow="Digital art", title="From the sketchbook", description="Maps, player characters and NPCs drawn for the table.", size="md") }}
      <a class="link-arrow nav-link" href="/art/">All drawings <span class="arrow-char" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
    <ul class="sketch-strip" role="list">
      {%- for item in sketches %}
      <li class="sketch-strip__item">
        <a class="tile" href="/art/#{{ item.slug }}">
          <div class="tile__media"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="{{ item.webpSrcset }}" sizes="{{ sketchSizes }}"><img src="{{ item.thumb }}" srcset="{{ item.srcset }}" sizes="{{ sketchSizes }}" width="{{ item.width }}" height="{{ item.height }}" alt="{{ item.alt }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></picture></div>
          <p class="tile__title">{{ item.title }}</p>
        </a>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}
